Previous study~\citep{10167495} uses inherently interpretable rule-based graph matching, but it still struggles with linguistic variability, ambiguous legal phrasing, and scalability to new regulations. A recent study~\citep{azeem2024multi} explores statistical machine learning and language model methods for the compliance detection task as text classification. However, it does not consider transparency and explainability factors such as model interpretability and reasoning.


