\section{Conclusion}
This work presented efficient algorithms for deriving the theoretically optimal coefficients for Newton-Schulz iteration. 
The practical effectiveness of CANS was demonstrated in accelerating the computation of the unitary polar factor, orthogonalization in the Muon optimizer, and fast retraction on the Stiefel manifold. We believe that our method can be useful for other applications as well, as it provides a general-purpose framework for finding optimized polynomials with desired accuracy.








