			$$\ov u_i(x^*)=u_i(S^*)\ge u_i(S_i,S^*_{-i})=\ov u_i(x_i,x^*_{-i})\,.$$
			Since the above holds true for every producer $i$ in $\mc N$ and every activation price $x_i$ in $[0,\hat p]$, we have that $x^*$ is a Nash equilibrium of the activation price game. 
