so that condition (a) and \eqref{eq:p_tilde} yield
$$x_i\le \ov p(x)=\frac{\gamma\hat p+\sum_{j=1}^n x_j}{n+\gamma}=\pa(x)\,,\;\forall i\in\mc N$$  
This proves that condition (a) implies that both \eqref{p*=pa} and condition (b) are satisfied.  

Conversely, if condition (b) is satisfied, then \eqref{eq:equilibrium_r} and \eqref{eq:aff_dem} imply that
$$\sum_{i=1}^n[\pa(x)-x_i]_+=\sum_{i=1}^n(\pa(x)-x_i)=\gamma(\hat p-\pa(x))=D(\pa(x))\,,$$
so that $\pa(x)$ satisfies equation \eqref{eq:equilibrium_r} for the market clearing price of the activation price game. Since equation \eqref{eq:equilibrium_r} admits $\ov p(x)$ as its unique solution, this implies that \eqref{p*=pa} is satisfied, 
so that condition (b) and \eqref{eq:p_tilde} yield
$x_i\le\pa(x)=\ov p(x)\,,$
for every producer $i$ in $\mc N$, thus proving that condition (a) is satisfied.  

Finally, observe that, for every $x$ such that conditions (a) and (b) are verified, we have that  $\pa(x)=\ov p(x)$, so that \eqref{eq:u_r} and \eqref{eq:ut_aa} imply that 
$$\ba{rcl}\apu_i(x)
&=&\ov p[\ov p(x)-x_i]_+-\frac{1}{2}[\ov p(x)-x_i]_+^2-C_i\left([\ov p(x)-x_i]_+\right)\\[7pt]
&=&\pa(x)(\pa(x)-x_i)-\frac12{(\pa(x)-x_i)^2}-\ca_i(\pa(x)-x_i)\\[7pt]
&=&\ua_i(x)\,,
\ea$$
for every producer $i$ in $\mc N$, thus proving \eqref{u=u*}. 
\end{proof}



