Finally, the proportion of reuniting moves by models OSP and SP does not significantly change as $\Delta t$ changes (Fig.~\ref{fig:l_m_reverse_robust}), which indicates that varying the time window is not able to make these models better predict the reuniting patterns observed in the real system. 

From these analyses, the main conclusion we are able to draw is that reuniting job moves are a robust feature of internal job mobility and which carry more information about the system than job moves that preserve occupational mobility or labor supply and demand. Furthermore, our exploration of the parameter $\Delta t$ does not indicate that our conclusion is an artifact of the way in which we select continuing teams on the basis of their longevity.

