\subsection{SQL Code Assistant}

SQL Code Assistant is designed to aid developers in writing SQL queries or SQL functions that access data models (schema, proto). Its testing involves the generated SQL queries/functions and test data instances that are often manually prepared and verified. This manual data generation often leads to incomplete data instances with partially filled schema elements neglecting complex and nested structures. This can lead to low test coverage, limiting the range of executable test queries. Furthermore, even a simple test case over a primitive (char) column can have low coverage if the data instances do not cover all the edge/branch cases under test.

