\section{Introduction}
\label{intro}
Traditional image/video compression algorithms rely on meticulously designed linear transforms. Recently, conventional methods have been increasingly challenged by emerging learning-based codecs that replace analysis and synthesis transforms in classical codecs with neural networks~\cite{balle2018variational, cheng2020image, he2022elic}. While achieving impressive performance gains, these autoencoder (AE)-based neural codecs often suffer from high decoding complexity and large number of network parameters, which limit their practical deployment on resource-constrained devices \cite{jiang2023mlic, wang2023evc}. In addition, they require training on extremely large datasets to ensure robust performance across diverse image distributions --- resources that are not always available. Addressing these issues to develop low-complexity and robust codecs with competitive rate-distortion (RD) performance remains a critical open challenge~\cite{yang2023introduction}.

