\paragraph{Interpretation of the design.}
\textcolor{black}{From the above visualizations, we interpret modulation as additional ``bias'', where concatenating neurons with a learned weight mask is equivalent to adding a flexible bias to the subsequent layers. This design demonstrates that the SuperMask network aims to encode images into the network structure, while ModNet introduces a flexible “adaptive bias” to enhance representation flexibility. As shown in Fig. \ref{vis_modulation_effect}, modulation outputs from different ModNet layers contribute varying compensatory information for image reconstruction.}

