The vertical axis of Figure~\ref{fig:perf} is in milliseconds so it could be argued,
in terms of absolute values, these 
are all similar. We would dispute that, saying that our evaluation times here  are near instant (just look at the labels). In practice, each evaluation could be very slow. For example, to check a proposed configuration for a Makefile, we may need to recompile an entire system, then run an extensive test suite.
In that context, the time differences in Figure~\ref{fig:perf} would become of great practical importance. 

 The smaller a code base, the faster newcomers can understand, adopt, apply, and adapt that code. 
 Hence it is important to note that 
 the code required to implement all our methods is orders of magnitude different in size.  
