\subsection{Narrows and Macros: Amarel's Pioneering Work}
In the 1960s, Amarel introduced the concept of narrows, small sets of variable assignments essential for reaching solutions in search problems \cite{Amarel1986}. Amarel’s research emphasized how large search spaces could be traversed efficiently by focusing on pathways (or macros) that connect critical narrows. His work highlighted the broader principle that optimization efforts should target a limited subset of important variables, a theme that recurs throughout AI and optimization.


