\subsection{Performance evaluation}
Experiments were conducted on a single NVIDIA A40 GPU. The fully supervised ResNet model, implemented in PyTorch and HuggingFace, was trained for 40 epochs. The fine-tuning of pre-trained Transformer-based models also utilised the HuggingFace Transformer framework \cite{wolf-etal-2020-transformers}, trained with a batch size of 16 for 20 epochs, early stopping is applied with a tolerance of 5 steps based on the evaluation set loss and accuracy. To standardise comparison with the ResNet model, we replaced the original \emph{Softmax} activation and \emph{CrossEntropyLoss} with \emph{LogSoftmax} activation and mean-reduced negative log-likelihood loss (\emph{NLLLoss}).
