L(p^{n+1}-2p^n+p^{n-1}) + DG ((p^n - p^{n-1}) + \alpha\tau p^n) - \alpha \tau S (p^n - p^{n-1}) = 0.
$$
Assume that $\hat{p}$ is a common eigenvector of $DG$ and $L$, and let $\beta \in [0,1]$ be defined by \eqref{eq_def_Omega}: $DG \hat{p} = (1-\beta) L \hat{p}$. Then $S\hat{p} = -\beta L\hat{p}$. Looking for solutions of the form
$$
p^n = \hat{p} \lambda^n,
$$
where $\lambda \in \mathbb{C}$ (here $p^n$ is the pressure at $n$-th layer and $\lambda^n$ stands for $\lambda$ to the power $n$), we come to
$$
(\lambda^2 - 2\lambda + 1) + (1-\beta)((\lambda-1) +\alpha\tau \lambda) + \alpha \beta \tau (\lambda - 1) = 0,
$$
which after simplification gives
$$
\lambda^2 - (1 + \beta - \alpha \tau) \lambda + (\beta - \alpha \beta \tau) = 0.
$$
Both roots of a quadratic equation of the form \mbox{$z^2 + bz+c=0$} belong to the unit circle if and only if $1 \ge c \ge |b|-1$. In our case, this condition expands to
$$
1 \ge \beta (1 - \alpha \tau) \ge  |1 + \beta - \alpha \tau| - 1.
$$
The left inequality holds, and the right one expands to
$$
1 + \beta - \alpha\beta\tau \ge 1+\beta - \alpha \tau \ge -1-(\beta - \alpha\beta\tau).
$$
Again, the left inequality holds, and the right one reduces to 
$$
(2 - \alpha\tau) (\beta + 1) = 0.
$$
Like in the original SRK method, we get the stability condition
$$
\alpha \le 2\tau^{-1}.
$$
\fi



