\item In our experiments, implicit SRK schemes usually show better accuracy than explicit and IMEX SRK schemes. The reason is that the term $\dot{H}(t)$ naturally appears at the implicit stage. So the use of an implicit SRK scheme reduces the discrepancy between the internal and boundary nodes. This effect is peculiar for this model problem.
\end{itemize}

